From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nura rc4i series <rc4i@nura.invalid>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: guacamole: describe the PM8150 PON reboot modes

pm8150.dtsi's pon@800 (compatible qcom,pm8998-pon) lists no mode-* magic
values, so reboot_mode_register() in qcom-pon.c finds nothing to write and
the PON reboot notifier ignores the reboot command string.  On this board
that means `systemctl reboot --reboot-argument=bootloader`, which becomes
reboot(2) with LINUX_REBOOT_CMD_RESTART2 and the argument "bootloader", is a
plain warm reset: the ABL re-boots the current slot instead of entering
fastboot.  The same applies to "recovery".

Describe the two modes on the board, with the values pm6150.dtsi and
pm6350.dtsi already use for the same PMIC family (0x01 recovery, 0x02
bootloader).  They are PMIC PON "soft reboot spare" reason codes that the
ABL reads back after the reset (PON_SOFT_RB_SPARE, GEN1 reason shift on this
part), so they have to match what the bootloader expects, not the kernel.

Nura-Category: device-dt
Nura-Origin: nura rc4i (reboot --reboot-argument=bootloader did not reach fastboot)
Upstream-Status: candidate
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-guacamole-nura.dtsi | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-guacamole-nura.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-guacamole-nura.dtsi
index aafda21..42ab586 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-guacamole-nura.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-guacamole-nura.dtsi
@@ -292,6 +292,19 @@
 	};
 };
 
+/*
+ * PM8150 PON reboot modes.  pm8150.dtsi's pon@800 carries no mode-* magic,
+ * so reboot_mode_register() has no entry for "bootloader" and
+ * `systemctl reboot --reboot-argument=bootloader` (reboot(2) RESTART2 with
+ * "bootloader") degrades to a plain warm reset: the ABL boots the current
+ * slot instead of entering fastboot.  Values and names match the PON nodes
+ * already describing this in pm6150.dtsi/pm6350.dtsi.
+ */
+&pon {
+	mode-recovery = <0x01>;
+	mode-bootloader = <0x02>;
+};
+
 /* Bluetooth WCN3990 on QUP13 UART, same rails as flame/hotdog. */
 &uart13 {
 	status = "okay";
